TENANCY.md: every show gets a site, and most of them are virtual
Capture, not construction. You were talking through something good while tired,
so this writes it down instead of acting on it.

## The idea, and why it is better than the framing so far

> what I would kinda want is for a virtualized empty version using our templates
> from the managed stuff to draw any other show that doesn't have a custom one.

Two tiers: a show with its own repository gets a `tenant` site; **every other
show gets one anyway**, generated from the show data this repository already
holds plus `member-site-core/`.

That inverts how the factory has been described. It was a thing a member opted
into. This makes a site **the default state of being a show here**, and a custom
repository the upgrade.

